   "requires": [],
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "A strong acid or base ionizes completely in water; a weak one ionizes only partly and sets up an equilibrium. Strength can be compared by [H₃O⁺] or [OH⁻], by pH or pOH, by percent ionization and by Ka or Kb, but the first three only at equal concentrations. Strength is not the same as concentration."
