   "id": "chem.ka",
   "name": "Acid ionization constant, Ka",
   "requires": [],
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "For a weak acid HA + H₂O ⇌ H₃O⁺ + A⁻, Ka = [H₃O⁺][A⁻]/[HA]; a larger Ka means a stronger acid. With an ICE table, x = [H₃O⁺] and Ka = x²/(C₀ − x). If x is at most 5 % of C₀, use C₀ − x ≈ C₀ so x = √(Ka·C₀); otherwise solve the quadratic. Then pH = −log x."
    },
    "am": {
     "text": "Ka = [H₃O⁺][A⁻]/[HA]፤ ትልቅ Ka ጠንካራ አሲድ ማለት ነው። በ ICE ሰንጠረዥ x = √(Ka·C₀) (5 % ደንብ ሲሟላ)።",
     "machine": true
    }
   },
